      section: "Common failure modes",
      content: "- **Letting power silently absorb a problem** by simply not returning to it —\n  the problem isn't resolved on the page, it's just never mentioned again\n  after the character becomes capable enough that a reader might expect it\n  to be trivial now.\n- **Solving a structural or emotional problem with a power-system shortcut**\n  (a spell that erases grief, a stat that removes trauma) which can work as\n  a deliberate, examined choice, but reads as a cheat if it arrives\n  unexamined.\n- **Never establishing any negative space at all**, so every problem in the\n  story is implicitly power-shaped, and the character's eventual\n  overwhelming strength quietly promises to make every future conflict\n  trivial too.",
