      section: "Evidence and detection limits",
      content: "Whether a specific scene, chapter, or book keeps or breaks an established\npromise requires reading and comparing prose for tone, stakes, and implied\ngenre — an interpretive judgment with no deterministic substitute. A future\ncoach could shortlist an opening passage and a comparison passage as\nevidence for the author's own review, but concluding that a promise was kept\nor broken is model-assisted, not something structured data can settle.\nSeries-level promise-consistency claims additionally require access to\nmultiple books' worth of manuscript, which most coaching sessions will not\nhave simultaneously.",
