      section: "Original micro-examples",
      content: "*Promise kept:* A story opens with a character narrowly avoiding eviction and\nworrying about a light bill. Its climax three hundred pages later still turns\non a resource shortage the character cannot simply out-power — the stakes\ngrew in scale but stayed the same kind.\n\n*Promise broken without signal:* The same opening, but by the climax the\ncharacter commands an army and the story's central tension has become a\npolitical succession crisis with no scene marking the shift from personal,\nsurvival-scale stakes to political, systemic ones.",
