      section: "Sources and confidence notes",
      content: "The series-longevity framing and the \"consistently delivers on its initial\npromise\" finding come from a single vendor's coded analysis of Reddit\ndiscussion ([[src.chapterchronicles.series-falloff]]), marked practitioner/\nreader consensus rather than controlled research; that same source frames\npromise consistency as a candidate connecting concept rather than a settled\nconclusion, and `docs/research-litrpg-craft-failures.md` explicitly raises,\nas an open question, whether promise consistency deserves to be the\nlibrary's organizing idea rather than one entry among many\n([[src.internal.litrpg-craft-failures-research]]). The general-craft framing\nof reader promise and stakes escalation draws on established craft writing\nabout market-aware structure ([[src.book.maass-writing-breakout-novel]]).\nThis record treats promise consistency as a strong, cross-source hypothesis\nworth prioritizing in coaching, not as a proven causal mechanism.",
